From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 18:56:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] power: a when condition's combinational outputs as functions
 of the inputs
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Power::findLeakagePower weighs each state dependent leakage group by
the duty of its when condition, found from a BDD with one variable per
pin, each weighted by its own pin's duty as if independent of the
others. Libraries that write the states over the inputs and the output,
"A * !Y" and "!A * Y" for an inverter, then weigh the states d^2 and
(1 - d)^2 instead of d and 1 - d: half the leakage at the default duty
of 0.5. asap7's INV, BUF, AO, AOI, OA and OAI cells, among others, are
written this way. Input internal power groups with such conditions
(asap7's AO/OA families) have the same error.

The combinational outputs a when condition names are now replaced by
their functions of the inputs (Cudd_bddCompose) before the duty is
found, for leakage, input internal power and the when of output
internal power. An output of a sequential cell or clock gate is state
and keeps its own duty, and a condition naming any port other than an
input or such an output is evaluated as before; conditions over inputs
only are unchanged.

power_when_output checks an inverter's leakage at duty d against
d * L(A=1) + (1 - d) * L(A=0) for d in {0, 0.1, 0.5, 0.9, 1}, an input
internal power condition naming the output, and that a NAND2's input
states and a flop's D and QN states are weighted as before.

asap7 RVT FF, one instance, report_power before -> after, leakage in
pW (input duty 0.1 / 0.5 / 0.9):

  INVx1     37.28 / 16.31 / 16.21 -> 43.15 / 32.62 / 22.08
  BUFx2     57.27 / 43.49 / 85.37 -> 72.93 / 86.98 / 101.03
  AOI21xp5  52.19 / 18.58 / 14.99 -> 60.57 / 40.40 / 16.66
  OAI21xp5  64.94 / 34.07 / 24.10 -> 66.90 / 59.75 / 32.27

AOI21xp5 and OAI21xp5 internal power moves +0.2% to +0.7%; XOR2xp5,
NAND2xp5, ICGx1 and TIEHIx1 are unchanged, and so is every other
OpenSTA regression.

Not upstreamed. Carried in bazel-orfs; retires on the //:bump onto an
OpenROAD whose OpenSTA has it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Øyvind Harboe <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
